    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2018-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The prime factorization is \\(23{,}232=2^6\\cdot3\\cdot11^2.\\) A divisor may use any exponent from \\(0\\) through \\(6\\) on \\(2\\), from \\(0\\) through \\(1\\) on \\(3\\), and from \\(0\\) through \\(2\\) on \\(11\\). Therefore, the number of positive divisors is \\((6+1)(1+1)(2+1)=42.\\)\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Prime-factorize \\(23,232\\).",
        "If \\(n=p^a q^b r^c\\), then its number of positive factors is \\((a+1)(b+1)(c+1)\\)."
      ],
